    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 80.05 efficiency score makes him our most potent asset against Melton. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a robust dynamic platoon advantage, positioning him to anchor our production in R and RBI. **Jackson Merrill** follows closely with a 75.27 score; he is primed for a massive outing against Lorenzen, as his elite SP_xERA matchup (+19% efficiency gain) and favorable platoon split suggest he is a prime candidate to generate the extra-base hits we need to maintain our offensive standing. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** offers a strong 73.66 score, serving as a critical engine for the Waves today by leveraging the vulnerability of Bieber.\n\nOur most difficult roster choice today involved **Miguel Vargas**, who landed on the bench with a 44.38 score despite a solid xwOBA. He was narrowly excluded because the volatility introduced by facing a high-caliber arm like Cole outweighed his base projection when compared to the immediate production expected from the likes of **Sam Antonacci** or **Andy Pages**. While **Miguel Vargas** remains a viable emergency option, we are leaning into the superior situational data of our starters. We are also monitoring the rainout situation regarding **Luis Robert Jr.**, whose postponement serves as a reminder to check for late-breaking weather alerts. While we are confident in our current configuration\u2014notably the aggressive deployment of **Nasim Nunez** and **Jacob Wilson** to capitalize on weak starting pitching\u2014we must remain vigilant, as the projected performances of **Liam Hicks** and **Coby Mayo** hover near our lower threshold for active consideration.",
